    "field": "Extreme event attribution",
    "problem": "Despite international agreements to limit warming to 1.5\u00b0C, there is a significant lack of literature assessing the impacts of this target and the potential benefits, specifically regarding the reduced frequency of extreme climate events compared to a 2\u00b0C warming scenario.",
    "method": "The proposed method analyzes climate extremes by selecting and pooling thousands of model-simulated years from existing CMIP5 ensembles that correspond to specific global warming levels (1.5\u00b0C and 2\u00b0C), creating large samples to statistically compare the changing frequency of extreme events between different climate scenarios.",
    "task": "The task is to use existing climate model simulations to analyze how limiting global warming to 1.5 \u00b0C, compared to 2 \u00b0C, affects the frequency of large-scale climate extremes in Australia.",
